    "originalInstructions": "1. Joint as for fricassee\n2. Pepper, salt, and flour the duck\n3. Heat good dripping in a frying-pan and fry a sliced onion to a light brown\n4. Take out the onion, put in the duck, and cook ten minutes, turning two or three times\n5. Put into a sauce-pan a cupful of stock or consomme, and while it is still cold lay in the jointed duck\n6. Cover and stew slowly until tender\n7. Season with pepper and salt, a tablespoonful of tomato catsup, and a dash of lemon-juice\n8. Simmer three minutes\n9. Stir in a tablespoonful of brown roux\n10. Cook a minute to thicken it\n11. Add a glass of sherry, and serve",
